From f8971fbe4099829e27cec62ad59d11cc150df06b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:17:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0124 -- narrowed multi-rect present from an
 engine dirty-box set

Consolidates 0124, 0128, 0129, 0130, 0131, 0132, 0134 and the cursor half of 0175.

Why. On AGS Quest present_update_window was 16.74 ms per frame: 460,800
bytes to VRAM at 27.5 MB/s, which is this machine's own LFB near-pointer
ceiling. A copy already at the bus limit cannot be made faster, only
smaller, so the engine's own invalidation is accumulated in screen space and
the present is narrowed to it. This needs no pixel comparison, so it
sidesteps patch 0102's gate (which switches the unchanged-frame compare off
above 100,000 bytes) and is why a 460,800-byte frame is narrowable at all.

Default is FULL. A present narrows only on a positive signal
(construct_game_scene() marks the frame as having come through the scene
path) and anything that demands a full frame latches it. A contributor nobody
accounted for then costs performance, never corruption. DOSAGS_DIRTY_PRESENT=0
turns narrowing off.

What each constituent is:
- 0124: screen-space dirty bbox from invalidate_rect_ds / _global, the
  scene_path signal, and the Present() narrowing itself.
- 0128: the bbox is in game coordinates and dst is in window coordinates
  (a letterboxed 640x360 in 640x480 differs by 60 rows), so the two were
  compared in different spaces. Translate first, and only for a pure offset.
  Per-cause rejection counters replace one latched string.
- 0129: a SET of boxes. The single bbox degenerates to the whole screen once
  two rects sit in opposite corners. Pushed through
  SDL_UpdateWindowSurfaceRects, which already took a count.
- 0130: per-row dirty accounting, to price a band design against the others
  off one run. Accounting only.
- 0131: clamp rects to the surface instead of rejecting them; the
  accumulator is fed un-clipped rects.
- 0132: the box cap is runtime (DOSAGS_DIRTY_BOXES, default 8, clamped to
  1..32) rather than a constant, so the knee is measured.
- 0134: a greedy pairwise merge priced at four thresholds. Accounting only;
  nothing merged is pushed.
- 0175 (part): dirty pixels attributed to the call site that asked for them
  (dirtysrc counters); this patch tags the cursor. The room/UI sprite tags
  share a hunk with the GUI skip and are in 0167.

Behaviour change: narrowing and the multi-rect push are ON by default.

Provenance of this export (2026-09-21): these edits sat uncommitted in the
vendor tree from patch 0123 onward, which is why every gate cell since said
build_dirty=1. They were made under one campaign-wide patch counter shared
with vendor/SDL, and each hunk carries its number in an in-source comment.
Intermediate states were never committed, so this patch is a hunk-level
partition of the final tree by concern, attributed by those comments -- not a
replay of the order the edits were made in, and its intermediate state was not
built on its own. The numbers named below are the ones found in its hunks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
